    answer: 'Original Medicare (Parts A and B) is administered directly by the federal government and allows you to see any doctor or hospital in the United States that accepts Medicare — without a referral and without prior authorization for most services. Medicare Advantage (Part C) is sold by private insurance companies that restrict you to a local HMO (Health Maintenance Organization) or PPO (Preferred Provider Organization) network and require prior authorization approval before many tests, procedures, and hospital admissions.',
  },
